<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchDaemon for the UPDATE HALF — `roomlerd update-helper`.

  Why this exists: `installer -pkg … -target /` requires root, and the
  DEFAULT macOS install is the per-user LaunchAgent alone (the privileged
  overlay daemon is opt-in). So a default install could never self-update:
  the agent either failed the install silently (pre-rc.469 it then exited 0
  and `KeepAlive{SuccessfulExit=false}` left the machine OFFLINE — field
  2026-08-25) or, after that fix, refused forever. This unit is the missing
  root half of updating, and nothing else: no enrollment, no control WS, no
  agent row — it resolves the PUBLIC release feed, verifies, installs, and
  exits. The agents merely signal it.

  It also removes the whole exit-to-update failure class on two-half Macs:
  no agent process is ever the installer's parent and none exits for an
  update — the pkg's postinstall re-bootstraps both halves, and no agent
  waits on the helper, so there is nothing to race.

  Wake sources, all three deliberate:
    RunAtLoad      — catch up right after boot / first install.
    StartInterval  — the periodic cadence (owned HERE, not by the agents;
                     one owner of "check+download+verify+install").
    WatchPaths     — the wake file a daemon touches for rc:agent.update or
                     its outage recheck, and `roomlerd self-update` for the
                     person's own ask. World-writable /var/tmp ON PURPOSE:
                     a per-user half is not root, and a wake is ADVISORY-ONLY:
                     a CHECK, never a choice of what gets installed (the
                     helper verifies the release; the install-storm cooldown
                     bounds spam). Since FR-151 it never counts or forces.
                     The helper keeps its own file there and reads a wake as
                     a change to it; its own consume starts no second run.

  Not KeepAlive: ThrottleInterval guards a crash-looping helper. FR-151: it
  reads both halves' live work before it installs, and after a defer stays
  up to read again at the recheck (an hour, R5b's two minutes) or a wake, at
  most once a minute, while launchd starts no second copy. It exits on the
  opt-out, a manual install, SIGTERM or 8 h awake, keeping its count; so
  does a run whose feed probe fails, and the next run is then StartInterval's
  unless a push, the person's ask, a boot or the outage recheck comes first.
  /etc/roomler/install-over-live-work makes it install with no reading.

  ⚠️ postinstall must NEVER bootout a RUNNING com.roomler.update: during an
  update postinstall is a grandchild of this very job, and a bootout kills
  the whole process group, `installer` included. It re-cycles an idle
  helper. A running one keeps its job and old plist, and one that waits for
  live work exits by itself within 5 s of a manual install (FR-151 D1).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.roomler.update</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Library/Roomler/roomlerd.app/Contents/MacOS/roomlerd</string>
        <string>update-helper</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- 6 h — mirrors the agents' old 4 h ± the reality that pushes cover
         the urgent case; the interval is the wedge-heal ceiling only. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>21600</integer>

    <key>WatchPaths</key>
    <array>
        <string>/private/var/tmp/roomler-update-check</string>
    </array>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/roomler/update.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/roomler/update.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>RUST_LOG</key>
        <string>info</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
